--- !u!114 &2046987868
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 2046987863}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 14f88726129a543db8d265bb0e06f3c1, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  sections:
  - id: 01
    title: Getting Started
    body: "Bitlings is a creature-collecting and battling game focused on growing
      a powerful team over time.\n\nThe core gameplay loop is:\n\nCatch \u2192 Train
      \u2192 Assign \u2192 Battle \u2192 Grow\n\n\u2022 Catch new Bitlings through
      encounters.\n\u2022 Train them by spending Growth Cores to increase their level.\n\u2022
      Assign them to job sites to earn resources and unlock battle passives.\n\u2022
      Battle using a turn-based system where types and Speed matter.\n\u2022 Grow
      your roster through evolutions, unlocks, and better jobs.\n\nUse this manual
      to learn what each major system does and how to use it.\n"
  - id: 02
    title: Monsters
    body: "Every Bitling has:\n\n\u2022 A Type (Fire, Water, Grass, etc.).\n\u2022
      A Level (raised with Growth Cores).\n\u2022 Base stats (like HP, Attack, Speed).\n\u2022
      Potential evolutions into stronger forms.\n\u2022 A small chance to appear
      as a shiny variant.\n\nLEVELING WITH GROWTH CORES\nBitlings do not gain XP
      directly. Instead, they grow using Growth Cores.\n\n\u2022 Each Growth Core
      fills part of a monster\u2019s training bar.\n\u2022 When the bar fills, the
      Bitling automatically levels up.\n\u2022 Higher levels require more Growth
      Cores to reach the next level.\n\u2022 Level ups improve stats and can unlock
      evolutions.\n\nYou mainly earn Growth Cores from the Gym job site.\n\nEVOLUTION\n\u2022
      Each Bitling line has a specific evolution level.\n\u2022 When a Bitling reaches
      that level via Growth Cores, it evolves automatically.\n\u2022 If a Bitling
      is already at its maximum level and you obtain another copy, the new one is
      added as a separate monster instead of evolving further.\n\nSHINY BITLINGS\n\u2022
      Shiny Bitlings are rare versions with different colors.\n\u2022 They are recorded
      as separate entries in the Codex.\n\u2022 Using Shiny Orbs and increasing Luck
      (from the Wyrm Den) can improve your chances to see shinies.\n\nTEAM MANAGEMENT\n\u2022
      Build a team using your owned Bitlings before starting encounters.\n\u2022
      A good team covers multiple Types to avoid hard weaknesses.\n\u2022 Use Medkits
      between encounters to heal your team.\n\u2022 Use Boosters (Attack, HP, Speed,
      etc.) when you need extra power for a tough fight.\n"
  - id: 03
    title: Battles
    body: "Bitlings uses a turn-based battle system.\n\nTURN ORDER\n\u2022 Turn order
      is based mainly on the Speed stat.\n\u2022 Faster monsters act before slower
      ones.\n\u2022 Speed Boosters and certain job passives can help your Bitlings
      move earlier.\n\nTYPE MATCHUPS\nEach Bitling has a Type. Attacks are stronger
      or weaker depending on the defender\u2019s Type. Choosing the right Type can
      greatly increase your damage or reduce damage taken.\n\nBelow are some example
      matchups:\n\nFire\n\u2022 Strong against: Grass, Bug, Ice\n\u2022 Weak against:
      Water, Rock\n\nWater\n\u2022 Strong against: Fire, Rock, Ground\n\u2022 Weak
      against: Grass, Electric\n\nGrass\n\u2022 Strong against: Water, Rock, Ground\n\u2022
      Weak against: Fire, Ice, Bug\n\nElectric\n\u2022 Strong against: Water, Sky,
      Alloy\n\u2022 Weak against: Ground, Rock\n\nIce\n\u2022 Strong against: Grass,
      Water, Sky, Wyrm\n\u2022 Weak against: Fire, Alloy\n\nRock\n\u2022 Strong against:
      Sky, Bug, Fire\n\u2022 Weak against: Water, Grass\n\nGround\n\u2022 Strong
      against: Electric, Corrupt\n\u2022 Weak against: Grass, Sky\n\nSky\n\u2022
      Strong against: Bug, Ground\n\u2022 Weak against: Electric, Rock\n\nBug\n\u2022
      Strong against: Grass, Umbral\n\u2022 Weak against: Fire, Rock\n\nSpecter\n\u2022
      Strong against: Umbral, Oracle\n\u2022 Weak against: Alloy\n\nUmbral\n\u2022
      Strong against: Oracle, Sky\n\u2022 Weak against: Bug, Specter\n\nOracle\n\u2022
      Strong against: Corrupt, Bug\n\u2022 Weak against: Umbral, Specter\n\nWyrm\n\u2022
      Strong against: Clash, Sky\n\u2022 Weak against: Alloy, Ice\n\nCorrupt\n\u2022
      Strong against: Alloy, Water\n\u2022 Weak against: Oracle, Ground\n\nClash\n\u2022
      Strong against: Bug, Ice\n\u2022 Weak against: Wyrm, Alloy\n\nAlloy\n\u2022
      Strong against: Wyrm, Ice\n\u2022 Weak against: Corrupt, Electric\n\nUse Types
      to your advantage: bring monsters that are strong against what you expect to
      face and avoid sending Bitlings into matchups they are weak against.\n"
  - id: 04
    title: 'Jobs, Types & Battle Passives '
    body: "Jobs are long-term activities where Bitlings work to generate resources
      and gain special battle bonuses.\n\nASSIGNMENT RULE\nJob passives only apply
      if a Bitling is:\n1) The correct Type for that job, and\n2) Currently assigned
      to that job site.\n\nIf you unassign a Bitling, it loses that job\u2019s battle
      bonus until it is assigned again.\n\nFATIGUE\nBitlings can become fatigued
      if they work in a job for too long without rest.\n\n\u2022 Fatigue reduces
      how many resources they produce.\n\u2022 Fatigue can also reduce the power
      of their job\u2019s battle bonus.\n\u2022 To recover, remove tired Bitlings
      from the job or rotate a fresh monster in.\n\nMONSTER JOB CHART\nEach job only
      accepts specific Types. Those Types are considered \u201Cbest\u201D for that
      job.\n\nGym\n\u2022 Allowed Type: Clash\n\u2022 Why: Clash Types are physical
      fighters, perfect for training and sparring.\n\nQuarry\n\u2022 Allowed Type:
      Ground\n\u2022 Why: Ground Types are sturdy laborers, ideal for moving earth
      and stone.\n\nMine\n\u2022 Allowed Type: Rock\n\u2022 Why: Rock Types excel
      at digging, mining, and handling heavy ore.\n\nPower Plant\n\u2022 Allowed
      Type: Electric\n\u2022 Why: Electric Types naturally manage power generation
      and energy flow.\n\nGrove\n\u2022 Allowed Type: Grass\n\u2022 Why: Grass Types
      tend forests, plants, and natural healing.\n\nForge\n\u2022 Allowed Type: Fire\n\u2022
      Why: Fire Types fuel the forges and handle high heat for crafting materials.\n\nWorkshop\n\u2022
      Allowed Type: Alloy\n\u2022 Why: Alloy Types are mechanical and precise, perfect
      for crafting tools and sigils.\n\nHarbor\n\u2022 Allowed Type: Water\n\u2022
      Why: Water Types specialize in fishing, shipping, and ocean work.\n\nCryo Lab\n\u2022
      Allowed Type: Ice\n\u2022 Why: Ice Types handle freezing, preservation, and
      temperature control.\n\nObservatory\n\u2022 Allowed Type: Oracle\n\u2022 Why:
      Oracle Types study data and stars, improving insight and survivability.\n\nContainment\n\u2022
      Allowed Type: Corrupt\n\u2022 Why: Corrupt Types manage volatile energies and
      containment tasks.\n\nWyrm Den\n\u2022 Allowed Type: Wyrm\n\u2022 Why: Wyrm
      Types explore deep tunnels and dens, uncovering rare finds.\n\nShadow Market\n\u2022
      Allowed Type: Umbral\n\u2022 Why: Umbral Types run risky trades, rare deals,
      and shiny odds manipulation.\n\nSanctum\n\u2022 Allowed Type: Specter\n\u2022
      Why: Specter Types channel spiritual energy, blessings, and protection.\n\nClinic\n\u2022
      Allowed Type: Sky\n\u2022 Why: Sky Types are fast responders, ideal for triage
      and recovery.\n\nExpedition\n\u2022 Allowed Type: Bug\n\u2022 Why: Bug Types
      are scouts and explorers, built for expeditions and discovery.\n\nJOB BATTLE
      BONUSES (OVERVIEW)\nEach job also grants a battle bonus to Bitlings who work
      there:\n\n\u2022 Gym: Increases Max HP based on hours worked, up to a cap.\n\u2022
      Forge: Increases damage of the first attack in battle.\n\u2022 Power Plant:
      Provides a Speed boost for the first turns.\n\u2022 Quarry: Increases Defense
      based on hours worked, up to a cap.\n\u2022 Grove: Grants small HP regeneration
      over multiple turns.\n\u2022 Workshop: Raises critical chance for the first
      few turns.\n\u2022 Harbor: Starts battle with a small shield and minor regeneration.\n\u2022
      Cryo Lab: Increases critical resistance.\n\u2022 Observatory: Grants flat crit
      chance and short-term protection at the start.\n\u2022 Containment: Reduces
      incoming damage up to a limit.\n\u2022 Clinic: Can trigger an emergency heal
      when HP drops low.\n\u2022 Wyrm Den: Grants a surge to Attack, often on the
      first attack.\n\u2022 Shadow Market: Reduces damage from the first incoming
      hit.\n\u2022 Sanctum: Provides starting shields and early damage reduction.\n\u2022
      Mine: Increases Attack based on hours worked.\n\u2022 Expedition: Provides
      special expedition rewards, often used for unlocks.\n"
  - id: 05
    title: 'Resources Overview '
    body: "Resources power your progress in Bitlings. Each one comes from specific
      jobs or systems and has a clear purpose.\n\nGrowth Cores\n\u2022 Comes from:
      Gym\n\u2022 Used for: Leveling Bitlings\n\u2022 Info: Fills a monster\u2019s
      training bar. When the bar is full, the Bitling levels up. Higher levels require
      more Growth Cores.\n\nAttack Boosters\n\u2022 Comes from: Mine\n\u2022 Used
      for: Temporary Attack increase\n\u2022 Info: Provides a short-term Attack boost
      for a limited number of uses.\n\nCapture Bands\n\u2022 Comes from: Cryo Lab\n\u2022
      Used for: Improving capture odds\n\u2022 Info: Increases your chance to successfully
      capture monsters for several attempts.\n\nCoins\n\u2022 Comes from: Quarry\n\u2022
      Used for: Upgrades\n\u2022 Info: General currency for upgrading jobs or related
      systems.\n\nEnergy\n\u2022 Comes from: Power Plant\n\u2022 Used for: Starting
      encounters\n\u2022 Info: Each encounter costs Energy. More Energy = more battles.\n\nGems\n\u2022
      Comes from: Achievement completion\n\u2022 Used for: Unlocking monster packs\n\u2022
      Info: A premium-like currency for special unlocks.\n\nHP Boosters\n\u2022 Comes
      from: Observatory\n\u2022 Used for: Temporary HP increase\n\u2022 Info: Adds
      flat HP for the next encounter for a limited number of uses.\n\nLuck\n\u2022
      Comes from: Wyrm Den\n\u2022 Used for: Increasing rare/shiny odds and improving
      drops\n\u2022 Info: Raises the chance of rare spawns and better rewards.\n\nLures\n\u2022
      Comes from: Harbor\n\u2022 Used for: Biasing encounter types and spawn rate\n\u2022
      Info: Increases the encounter weight of certain Types for several encounters.\n\nMaterials\n\u2022
      Comes from: Forge\n\u2022 Used for: Upgrading job sites\n\u2022 Info: Mostly
      spent on permanent improvements to jobs.\n\nMedkits\n\u2022 Comes from: Grove\n\u2022
      Used for: Healing the team between battles\n\u2022 Info: Restore HP outside
      of combat.\n\nRest Charges\n\u2022 Comes from: Clinic\n\u2022 Used for: Restoring
      Energy or skipping timers\n\u2022 Info: Let you bypass waiting or refill key
      resources.\n\nShiny Orbs\n\u2022 Comes from: Shadow Market\n\u2022 Used for:
      Boosting shiny chance\n\u2022 Info: Temporarily increases the odds of encountering
      shiny Bitlings.\n\nSigils\n\u2022 Comes from: Workshop\n\u2022 Used for: Applying
      Type resistance during encounters\n\u2022 Info: Reduce damage from certain
      Types for a limited number of uses.\n\nSpeed Boosters\n\u2022 Comes from: Containment\n\u2022
      Used for: Temporary Speed increase\n\u2022 Info: Helps a Bitling act earlier
      in turn order for a battle.\n\nBlessing Tokens\n\u2022 Comes from: Sanctum\n\u2022
      Used for: Sanctum blessings and run-wide perks\n\u2022 Info: Spent to apply
      powerful effects that can last across multiple encounters.\n\nShards (if used)\n\u2022
      Comes from: Expedition\n\u2022 Used for: Special unlocks such as packs or shop
      items\n\u2022 Info: A higher-level resource earned from exploration.\n"
  - id: 06
    title: 'Titles & Boosters '
    body: "Titles and Boosters let you customize how your Bitlings fight and work.\n\nTITLES\nTitles
      are permanent traits or labels that can be attached to Bitlings. Examples include:\n\n\u2022
      Titles that increase basic stats (Attack, HP, Speed).\n\u2022 Titles that give
      conditional bonuses (stronger when low HP, etc.).\n\u2022 Titles that improve
      job performance or job-related bonuses.\n\nOnce you unlock a Title, you can
      assign it to a Bitling to change how that monster behaves in battle or at a
      job.\n\nBOOSTERS\nBoosters are consumable items you use before or during encounters
      to gain short-term advantages.\n\nCommon examples:\n\u2022 Attack Boosters:
      Raise your Attack stat for the next encounter or a few turns.\n\u2022 HP Boosters:
      Add bonus HP to help you survive.\n\u2022 Speed Boosters: Increase Speed so
      you can act earlier.\n\u2022 Sigils: Improve resistance against specific Types.\n\nUse
      Titles for long-term builds and Boosters for short-term bursts of power in
      tough fights.\n"
  - id: 07
    title: 'Codex & Monster Unlocks '
    body: "The Codex is your in-game encyclopedia for everything you have discovered.\n\n\u2022
      Each discovered Bitling is recorded with its name, Type, and details.\n\u2022
      Undiscovered Bitlings appear as ??? until you obtain or encounter them.\n\u2022
      Locked entries often have hints, such as \u201CDefeat a certain enemy\u201D
      or \u201CReach a certain area.\u201D\n\u2022 Shiny forms and evolved forms
      are treated as separate entries once discovered.\n\u2022 Newly discovered entries
      can be marked as \u201CNew\u201D until you view them.\n\nFILTERS\nThe Codex
      can be filtered and sorted to help you find what you need:\n\n\u2022 Sort A\u2013Z
      or Z\u2013A.\n\u2022 Filter by Type (Fire, Water, Grass, etc.).\n\u2022 Show
      only unlocked or only locked entries.\n\nUse the Codex to track your collection,
      plan what to hunt next, and see how close you are to full completion.\n"
  - id: 08
    title: Progression
    body: "Progression in Bitlings is mainly driven by:\n\n\u2022 Growth Cores and
      monster levels.\n\u2022 Job usage and job upgrades.\n\u2022 Titles and monster
      customization.\n\u2022 Achievements and long-term goals.\n\nGROWTH CORES AND
      LEVELS\n\u2022 Each Bitling has a training bar.\n\u2022 Growth Cores fill that
      bar.\n\u2022 When the bar is full, the Bitling levels up automatically.\n\u2022
      Higher levels require more Growth Cores.\n\u2022 Leveling increases stats and
      may unlock evolutions.\n\nJOB PROGRESSION\n\u2022 Jobs can be upgraded using
      resources like Materials and Coins.\n\u2022 Assigning the correct Types to
      each job maximizes resource production and battle bonuses.\n\u2022 Rotating
      monsters and managing fatigue keeps your workforce and battle team strong.\n\nACHIEVEMENTS\n\u2022
      Achievements track long-term goals (captures, battles, jobs used, etc.).\n\u2022
      Some achievements reward resources such as Gems.\n\u2022 Your overall completion
      progress increases as you earn more achievements.\n\nBy combining Growth Cores,
      jobs, Titles, and achievements, you steadily make your Bitlings stronger and
      unlock more of what the game has to offer.\n"
